title: HAProxy Backdoor Trigger Path Request (DPRK ted implant)
id: f4e2a1b7-8c3d-4e5f-9a0b-6d7e8f1c2a3b
status: experimental
description: Detects HTTP requests to the hidden command-channel trigger path used by the DPRK-linked 'ted backdoor' implanted in HAProxy binaries. The path /favorite_list_2x_m500_ico.jpg activates the implant's full command set when contacted with a specially crafted request.
references:
  - https://gbhackers.com/dprk-linked-hackers-backdoor-haproxy-servers-to-spy-on-south-korean-organizations/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026-09-08
tags:
  - attack.t1100
  - attack.t1071
logsource:
  category: webserver
  product: haproxy
detection:
  selection_path:
    cs-uri-statement|contains: '/favorite_list_2x_m500_ico.jpg'
  selection_method:
    cs-method: 'GET'
  condition: selection_path and selection_method
falsepositives:
  - Unlikely in normal HAProxy operation; any match is highly suspicious
level: high
